[2026-09-06T03:40:00Z] review follow-up (Codex review of 3dcfaa5, six findings): all six confirmed against the code and the committed records, all six fixed. (1) The cluster-level exact test was being computed against control A, whose two random directions are drawn afresh for every item, while the lens arm gives every unit of a cluster the identical source direction, so the two arms' cluster totals are not exchangeable; cluster_control.py was written and run (see the line above) and analyse.py now reports cluster_tests_shared_control beside cluster_tests. Against the cluster-matched control the held-out probabilities are H17a 0.0041 (pairs, at its resolution), 0.037 (rank-one questions) and 0.0041 (layer 9), and H17 5.1e-05 by source concept and 2.09e-07 by source and target at the protocol setting, all unchanged in value; pooled over both source rules they move from 1.88e-06 to 3.76e-06 and from 8.6e-10 to 9.46e-09, and the lens source rule alone from 0.0123 to 0.0247 and from 4.57e-04 to 2.29e-03. (2) The test's resolution now counts only the clusters whose draws are not all equal: H17b's held-out resolution moves from 1.53e-05 to 0.25 and its all-items resolution from 2.33e-10 to 0.00391, and H17's six move likewise; no probability changes. (3) measure_disturbance.py now divides by the untouched residual streams of every patched layer taken together; the H17 ratios move from 0.34, 0.23 and 0.13 to 0.194, 0.134 and 0.074 and the lens maximum from 1.47 to 0.842, while every change size is identical to the 2026-09-05 file to three decimals. (4) Decision item 2's H17b held-out probability corrected from 0.5 to 0.25. (5) run_swaps.py writes its record file through a temporary file and moves it into place only after the whole plan is scored, and analyse.load refuses a record file whose row count does not match the plan in its provenance (checked: 35,280, 18,600 and 14,112 rows, each equal to its plan; a truncated copy is refused with the shortfall named). (6) lib_exp0