[2026-09-06T04:01:19.430741Z] cluster_control.py h17 h17a: exit 0, 107.5 s, 1416 conditions. Four cluster-matched control arms for the cluster-level exact tests: shared_source (one random source direction per cluster, an independent random target direction per item), shared_pair (both shared across the units that share source and target), by_token (every random direction seeded by the token it stands in for, so reuse across units matches the lens arm's exactly) and, for H17, mirrored (token-seeded, and the control picks its own target, and for the lens source rule its own source, by the battery's layer-8 rule applied to its own random directions, scored on its own chosen concept). The lens arm was re-run beside them and reproduces the committed record files on every scored unit at these settings. Wrote output/cluster_control_records_v2.csv and output/cluster_control_provenance_v2.json; no committed file was overwritten.

[2026-09-06T04:20:00Z] review follow-up (second Codex review of the day, of 093454d, four findings): all four confirmed and all four answered. (1) Grouping the scored units by source concept, or by source and target concept, leaves different groups sharing a lens direction: in the held-out output half of H17 three groups swap out of ' football' and four groups with different sources swap into ' dolphin', and ' strawberry' is a source in two frames and a target in two others. analyse.py now also groups the units into the connected components of the graph that joins two units using the same lens direction in either role, and reports those tests beside the others. Component counts on the held-out half: H17 output rule 7 (6 informative), H17 lens rule 5 (3), H17 pooled 4 (4), H17a 1 (1), H17b 8 (1) and 13 over all 16 items (3). Floors: 1 in 729 for the H17 protocol reading, 1 in 81 pooled, 1 in 3 for H17a, 1 in 4 for H17b held out. (2) The cluster-matched control of the previous commit redrew the target direction per item where the lens arm reuses one direction across items (four football to cricket frames, two blue to yellow). cluster_control.py gained the arm randdir_by_token, which seeds every random direction by the token it stands in for, and the arm randdir_mirrored (see 3), and wrote output/cluster_control_records_v2.csv, which reproduces the 816 rows of the first run byte for byte and adds 600. Against the token-seeded control the H17 pooled by-source-and-target figure moves from 9.46e-09 to 1.72e-09 and the lens rule's from 2.29e-03 to 4.57e-04, while every protocol figure and every H17a figure is unchanged; that control succeeded on one held-out frame in 168 draws. (3) The layer-8 target selection is pre-registered design (specification section 5.1, committed 47efd8d), so the finding is about interpretation, not a coding fault: every H17 probability except the mirrored ones is conditional on the lens-selected targets. The mirrored control ran inside the same 108 seconds: it gives every candidate a random direction of that candidate's lens length seeded by the candidate's token, picks its target (and, for lens-rule frames, its source) by the same layer-8 rule applied to those directions, and is scored on its own chosen concept. It chose the lens arm's target on 21 of 168 draws and succeeded 0 of 42 times on held-out output-rule frames and 2 of 42 on held-out lens-rule frames. Against it the H17 protocol reading is unchanged at 0.00137 by component, 5.08e-05 by source and 2.09e-07 by source and target; the pooled reading is unchanged at 0.0123 by component; the lens rule weakens from 0.037 to 0.0741 by component. (4) lib_exp016.load_lens now catches the missing jlens package and names the clone, checkout and install of anthropics/jacobian-lens at 581d398613e5602a5af361e1c34d3a92ea82ba8e, and the reproduction section carries the same step. analyse.py h17 h17a h17b re-run (exit 0): every value that existed before is byte identical, and the only additions are the by-component entries and the two new test blocks. make_tables.py output re-pasted into RESULTS_EXP016.md. make_figures.py re-run (exit 0): both PNG files byte identical to the committed ones. No swap condition of the three committed batteries was re-run and no committed output file was overwritten.

