[2026-09-06T05:10:00Z] review follow-up (third Codex review of the day, of f871571, two findings): both confirmed and both answered. (1) The tuning and held-out halves share lens directions: 19 of the 36 concepts H17 uses appear in both halves, all 14 of H17a's do, and 3 of H17b's 16 do, so the setting chosen on the tuning half is not independent of the held-out outcomes under the null. analyse.component_split joins frames that share a concept in either role, which divides H17's 84 frames into 4 groups of 24, 20, 20 and 20, one per category, and deals whole groups alternately by smallest frame identifier, giving a tuning half of 40 frames and a held-out half of 44 with no concept in common. Redoing the whole selection there chooses layers 6-7-8, strength 2.0, all, source rule output; the held-out result is 20 of 22 against 1 of 44 for control A, beside the committed split's 18 of 21 against 0 of 42, and both clear the registered thresholds. H17a admits no such split, its 50 pairs forming one group over a single pool of 14 countries. (2) The component product is not valid against the mirrored control, which chooses its own concepts: in this battery the crossing is narrow, since the control always chooses inside the frame's own category and the components are exactly the four categories, but ' orange' belongs to both the fruit and the colour word list, so one draw can act in two components. Codex's cited example, ' grape' at seed 0, does not cross a component: it is only a fruit, and no target picked at seed 0 crosses a component boundary. global_draw_control.py replaces the product with a Monte Carlo randomisation test over 499 draws, one draw being one random direction per concept seeded by token, layer and draw index with the mirrored target selection applied, a whole held-out set scored under each draw: 21 frames under the committed split at layers 7-8-9 give 0.002 (0 of 499 draws reaching the lens arm's 18), 22 frames under the component-respecting split at layers 6-7-8 give 0.002 (0 of 499 reaching 20), and H17b's 8 held-out items give 0.002 (0 of 499 reaching 1). The lens arm was re-run for every set and reproduces the committed record files exactly. Two short timing probes at 4 and 64 draws preceded the full run and their lines are above; the full run replaced their output before anything was committed. analyse.py h17 h17a h17b re-run (exit 0), make_tables.py output re-pasted into RESULTS_EXP016.md, make_figures.py re-run (exit 0). No swap condition of the three committed batteries was re-run and no committed output file was overwritten.
